## 2026-08-23 — Orca ADE Integration (OpenCode harness)

**User goal:** run the seven global agents as separate sessions inside Orca ADE
(onorca.dev, Stably AI), OpenCode as harness.

**Verified from Orca docs/CLI reference:**
- OpenCode ships preconfigured in Orca (auto-setup, status). Agent combobox = process launch.
- Global `~/.config/opencode/agents/*.md` apply in every worktree (user-level config,
  cwd-independent). Zero per-project config required for persona availability.
- Per-agent launch-argument overrides exist (Settings -> Agents); a non-empty custom value
  is treated as explicit user override.
- Quick Commands (terminal command presets) are project-scoped and mobile-synced but live
  in app storage, not repository files.
- Orchestration (`worker-start --agent opencode`) supports tasks/dispatches/gates;
  per-worker `--model`/`--effort` limited to Claude/Codex/Cursor. No documented flag pins an
  OpenCode sub-agent per dispatched worker; workaround = role contract in task spec or a
  global `--agent <persona>` argument override.

**Deliverable:** `docs/ORCA_INTEGRATION.md` — prerequisites, three usage patterns
(single-pane persona switching / parallel panes via Quick Commands / supervised
orchestration with limitations stated), verification checklist. No speculative `orca.yaml`
created: only `scripts.*` and `worktree.sharedDirectories` are confirmed schema keys today;
project has no setup scripts worth wiring during preplan.

**Manual steps that remain for the user (app-storage, not file-based):** install Orca,
enable OpenCode in Settings -> Agents, optionally paste the seven Quick Command rows, and
enable Experimental -> orchestration if Pattern C is wanted.

