## 2026-08-23 — Token Accounting System

**User requirement:** per-agent consumption ledgers, unified root total refreshed on
merges to main, token disclosure in every PR, and a README footer stating the final
total ("This application was made with N tokens").

**Design constraint (stated to user):** an agent cannot introspect its own usage
mid-session; authoritative numbers are the OpenCode harness session totals shown at
session end. The protocol forbids estimates.

**Delivered:**
1. `.agents/agent_<name>_consumed_tokens.md` x7 — one table per agent
   (Date/Time | Input | Output | Session Total | Description <=40 chars).
2. `scripts/token_ledger.py` — `log` appends validated rows (rejects descriptions over
   40 chars and unknown agents); `summarize` rebuilds the root total from all ledgers
   and auto-patches the README footer line.
3. Root `total_tokensconsumed.md` — per-agent sessions/in/out/total table + grand total,
   regenerated on every merge to main by the merging agent (rule 6.2 of AGENTS.md).
4. `README.md` created for the repo, ending with the required sentence
   (currently "0 tokens" until the first logged session).
5. `.github/pull_request_template.md` — mandatory Tokens Consumed table whose PR TOTAL
   must equal the sum of ledger rows included in that PR.
6. `AGENTS.md` section 6 "Token Accounting Rules (Mandatory)" — session-end logging,
   merge-time summarize, PR disclosure, file ownership map.

**Tested:** valid row append; >40-char description rejection; unknown-agent rejection;
summarize zero-state generation; README footer patch. Test row reverted before commit;
ledgers start empty at zero.

**Compliance note:** enforcement is procedural (AGENTS.md mandate + PR template + script
validation), not technical. A future hardening option is an OpenCode plugin that reads
session usage events and appends rows automatically; deferred until after plan lock.
